\n\nAlan ROBB claimed the men's title in 05:40:43, ahead of Cavin WOODWARD (05:49:00) and Dave ROGERS (05:52:00). Lettie VAN ZYL won the women's race in 09:05:00, followed by Alet TEN TUSSCHER (09:35:00).\n\nLettie VAN ZYL set a new women's course record of 09:05:00, surpassing Betty CAVANAGH's 10:08:00 from 1975. Women's runner-up Alet TEN TUSSCHER's 09:35:00 also beat the previous women's record.\n\nFrom a field of 1,408 entries, 1,408 runners completed the course for a 100.0% finish rate. The field comprised 1,403 men and 5 women (0.4% female). The average finish time was 08:57:48.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 220 Silver, 1,178 Bronze. 527 runners (37.4%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Des PATERSON in 10:59:00.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1973, the field was 14.8% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 20% of the finishers, with 1,127 seniors (avg 08:55:10) and 277 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.1}